            <div xml:id="d647">

                <pb facs="0678" n="574" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg574"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/719.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-05-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 12, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The American Minister will be invited to attend the Te Deum Mass on the 14th
                    instant in honor of the election of President Oreste, and to attend a reception
                    after the Mass. Being Dean of the Diplomatic Corps, which will attend these
                    functions, his absence therefrom would be injurious to American influence.
                    Attendance at these functions signifies recognition. Asks instructions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Furniss</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
